WEBVTT

NOTE
This file was generated by Descript <www.descript.com>

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:02.630
Abraham: Even in the most
efficient well-run companies,

00:00:02.990 --> 00:00:04.900
teams can be affected by conflict.

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:08.729
This may involve a clash of team members
over their contributions to a shared

00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:12.610
project or team leaders who have battled
over their positions with managers who

00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:16.619
don't see eye to eye with them or simply
a clash of personalities within the team.

00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:19.850
Whatever the source of the
conflict, it often involves a

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:22.950
breakdown in communication and
trust and can cause resentment.

00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:27.069
Conflict should be addressed before
it gets out of hand, and this can

00:00:27.070 --> 00:00:30.459
be done using proactive strategies
as conflict often starts with small

00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:32.349
disagreements that escalate fast.

00:00:32.769 --> 00:00:35.330
Nicole: So, what are the signs
of conflict within a team?

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:39.110
Things that can suggest conflict
are the members of the team’s

00:00:39.110 --> 00:00:43.310
body language, facial expressions,
and tone of voice in discussions.

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:47.389
Team leaders and managers who know
the team members should be able to

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:49.710
spot any changes in the team dynamic.

00:00:50.420 --> 00:00:52.050
Abraham: What can be done to resolve this?

00:00:52.980 --> 00:00:56.400
Using an intermediary or trusted
third party that both sides can

00:00:56.400 --> 00:01:00.030
have faith in, can help with
resolving conflict by being fair and

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:02.100
impartial and identifying the issues.

00:01:02.650 --> 00:01:06.699
By remaining objective they can give
everyone involved the time and opportunity

00:01:06.700 --> 00:01:10.550
to present their own perspective on
events associated with the conflict.

00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:13.819
Dominant individuals should not
be allowed to bully more reserved

00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:17.040
members of the team, and everyone
should be able to have their say.

00:01:18.110 --> 00:01:20.429
Nicole: Let's look at what
process should be followed.

00:01:21.090 --> 00:01:24.620
First, team members should be
spoken to individually and each

00:01:24.630 --> 00:01:26.310
should be asked the same question.

00:01:26.679 --> 00:01:29.979
They should also be made aware that
all discussions are confidential.

00:01:30.510 --> 00:01:33.920
Individuals should be allowed to put
their points of view forward in their

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:36.040
own time without making assumptions.

00:01:36.630 --> 00:01:41.139
Once the intermediary or facilitator
understands the different perspectives,

00:01:41.490 --> 00:01:45.489
then they need to bring the different
parties together and encourage them to

00:01:45.490 --> 00:01:49.799
discuss the issues between themselves
in a calm and non-confrontational

00:01:49.799 --> 00:01:54.019
manner, giving opportunity to listen
to and respect each other’s views.

00:01:54.019 --> 00:01:57.780
If the conflict affects the
whole team, then this discussion

00:01:57.789 --> 00:01:59.190
should involve the whole team.

00:02:00.039 --> 00:02:03.330
Once the grievances have been
aired then a plan should be drawn

00:02:03.330 --> 00:02:07.550
up to detail and agree on actions
for resolution and reconciliation.

00:02:08.190 --> 00:02:11.109
This should be followed up by
getting feedback on how things

00:02:11.320 --> 00:02:12.880
are progressing going forward.

00:02:13.430 --> 00:02:17.179
Sometimes by airing the grievances
that may have started the conflict,

00:02:17.389 --> 00:02:20.869
things can be resolved quite
amicably to suit all parties.

00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:25.270
If, however, a resolution to the
conflict cannot be reached, then

00:02:25.270 --> 00:02:29.732
formal procedures may need to be taken
and disciplinary action may follow

00:02:29.732 --> 00:02:32.000
depending on the nature of the conflict.

